The antechamber to this side of the divine meeting room is lush and detailed, 
with many works of art, attributed to the skill of Casimir and his manipulation
of the scripts of time. They depict many events of O'len, the world that is, as
well as some events which came to pass in other reflections of O'len, along
different lines of infinite play. One of particular interest depicts the 
firstborn of Sabbthiel, and the divine grandparents watching as the two raise
their child, Ruotsalainen, teaching him the ways of infinite play and respect
for possibility as the only true good. The scene grows happily into one of 
peace and tolerance. Sadly, allowing for infinite play and possibility also 
allows that the second tableau, located opposite said depiction, portraying the
death of the firstborn at the hand of their child and the inexorable 
destruction of infinite play that follows along such a doomed path. The meeting
room of the divines lies east of where you stand, while a staircase wraps 
around the room, leading to a balcony which overlooks both the room and the
garden without.
